You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput Spring Boot service gradually exhausts Old Generation space over several days, causing severe GC pauses and an eventual `OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space`. You inspect the following worker implementation running inside a pooled `@Async` executor:

java
@Service
public class TransactionAuditService {
    private final ThreadLocal<List<AuditRecord>> localBatch = 
        ThreadLocal.withInitial(ArrayList::new);

    @Async("fixedThreadPoolTaskExecutor")
    public void bufferAndSend(AuditRecord record) {
        List<AuditRecord> batch = localBatch.get();
        batch.add(record);
        if (batch.size() >= 500) {
            flushToRemote(batch);
            batch.clear();
        }
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where a Spring Data JPA batch job processing 1,000,000 database rows throws `java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space` after processing approximately 150,000 records. The service method is structured as follows:

java
@Service
public class CustomerMigrationService {
    @PersistenceContext
    private EntityManager entityManager;

    @Autowired
    private CustomerRepository customerRepository;

    @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRED)
    public void migrateAllCustomers() {
        customerRepository.findAllByStatus("ACTIVE").forEach(customer -> {
            customer.setTier(calculateTier(customer));
            // Updates applied to managed entity
        });
    }
}
